{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let store = try SegmentStore()","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Write-through."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A tracker’s worker writes each record as it reaches it, before publishing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, with one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write()"},{"type":"text","text":", off the tracking caller’s thread, so the record survives the app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"crashing or being killed from then on. The store makes the log durable against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"power loss too ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"type":"text","text":") once per batch, before the batch is delivered, and whenever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()"},{"type":"text","text":" is called: call it, after the tracker’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":", as the app moves to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"background or terminates."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record whose write fails (the disk is full, say) is kept in memory only, and reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and so is one whose event’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"encode(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" throws."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"What is kept.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Every event "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiscoveredEvent.all"},{"type":"text","text":" lists, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" structs of every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module the program links and the library’s own, or only the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" types in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Of the discovered types that share a name, only the one at the highest version is kept: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"version the program tracks. Events of any other type are kept in memory only: they are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered in this run like any other, are never written, and are lost if the app ends first."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The first record of each such type is reported as "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type left out by mistake, such as one that conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand, shows up."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A recovered record’s context."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A record keeps these keys of its context, written in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record’s own bytes, so a record recovered after a relaunch reaches destinations as it was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracked:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a vendor destination sends it under the same identity as the first time;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SampleRateKey"},{"type":"text","text":", so it is weighted by the rate it was sampled at;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ScreenKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"DeviceKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NetworkKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so it is attributed to where it was tracked, not to the run that uploads it.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A locale is kept as its identifier, so a preference the identifier doesn’t spell is lost.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The store writes these keys whatever set them, so don’t build a screen name, or an app or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"device value, from user data."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A key the record didn’t have comes back absent. No other key is kept, so a recovered record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is otherwise in the top-level "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ServiceContext"},{"type":"text","text":": not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"VendorIdentifierKey"},{"type":"text","text":", which Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never stores; not a key of the app’s own, such as an account’s, which the store can’t tell"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from an identifier; and not the trace context, as its span ended with the earlier run."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Deleting.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A segment is deleted as a whole once every record in it is delivered, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"log whose records are all delivered holds no files. A record’s context goes with its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"segment: the store keeps no session apart from the records tracked in it. A segment kept","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for one undelivered record keeps its delivered ones too, sessions and all. Only recovery","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rewrites a segment: one still holding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records after it drops some (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":") is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rewritten without them, so each drop is reported once. Should the rewrite fail, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"segment is kept as it was and the next launch reports those drops again.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reading back."}]},{"type":"text","text":" When a destination’s full buffer drops a batch on its way through a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivery, the delivery reads that batch’s records back from the log once the destination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has caught up, reading each segment they are in once, and hands them to it in this run,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each in the context it was tracked in, which the delivery keeps. A record the bound dropped"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before the read finished isn’t read back, and one that can’t be read or decoded is logged"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and waits for a later launch."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Bound."}]},{"text":" The log never holds more than ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"byteBound"},{"text":" bytes. When a record wouldn’t fit, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"oldest segments are deleted until it does, and each one deleted with records not yet","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered yields a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","isActive":true},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","isActive":true},{"text":". A record too large for an empty log","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is kept in memory only.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Recovery.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" A store opened on a directory recovers the records earlier runs left there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a tracker given the store delivers them first. Each segment is cut at its first torn or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"corrupt record, keeping every intact record before it, and the bytes cut off are reported.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A segment comes back whole, delivered records and all. Each record a delivery had started on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comes back with ","type":"text"},{"code":"isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" set, as it may have reached a destination already: one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered before the app ended, or one delivered just as it ended, before the store could","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delete its segment. A record whose delivery mark can’t be written is held back from that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivery, so it is never sent twice unannounced, and delivered on a later launch.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Other versions."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A segment a newer release of the app wrote, in a later version of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format, is left on disk untouched after a rollback, for that release to deliver: this one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"neither reads it nor counts it toward the bound. A segment in an earlier version, which this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one can’t read, is deleted and reported as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/corruption(byteCount:)","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Changed event types.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Each record’s event is a map of its properties by name, so a record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"written before its type changed still reads: a property removed since is skipped, an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optional one added since is "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and one with a default value added since has it. A record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stored at another "},{"code":"Event.schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" than its type’s now is dropped without being read and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reported as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"One at the same version that can’t be read all the same, after a required property was added"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or a property’s type changed without raising the version, is dropped and reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Open one store per directory at a time; two would delete each other’s segments. Copies of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store share its log.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Stores","generated":true,"title":"Stores","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStoreError","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"]]},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:11Persistence12SegmentStoreV","remoteSource":{"fileName":"SegmentStore.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Persistence\/SegmentStore.swift#L89"},"modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"SegmentStore","roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size, until they are delivered."}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/byteCount","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/directory","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/pendingRecordCount"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/append(_:)","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/takeRecoveredRecords()"]},{"anchor":"Type-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Type Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultByteBound","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultDirectory"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/RecordStore":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where a tracker keeps each record until it is delivered, so records survive the app ending."}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","title":"RecordStore","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/recordstore","role":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/defaultDirectory":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Where a store keeps its segments unless it is given a directory.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/defaultdirectory","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultDirectory","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FilePath","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SystemPackage8FilePathV"}],"title":"defaultDirectory","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultDirectory"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/takeRecoveredRecords()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The records of the segments earlier runs left, oldest first, with "},{"code":"isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" set on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each one a delivery had started on; later calls return none."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"takeRecoveredRecords","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventRecord","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events11EventRecordV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/takeRecoveredRecords()","title":"takeRecoveredRecords()","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/takerecoveredrecords()","role":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/byteCount":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The bytes the log holds on disk: every segment’s header, records and delivery marks."}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/bytecount","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"byteCount","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"byteCount","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/byteCount"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/notPersisted(event:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A record of the event named "},{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" was kept in memory only because its type isn’t one of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the store’s "},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": its records are delivered in this run, but never written, so they are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lost if the app ends first. Reported once per type, on its first record, for as long as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store lives; a type left out by mistake is added to "},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"notPersisted"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"event"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","kind":"symbol","title":"DropReport.notPersisted(event:)","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/notpersisted(event:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DropReport","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Records a store dropped before they were delivered, and why.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DropReport","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"DropReport","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/corruption(byteCount:)":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/corruption(bytecount:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/corruption(byteCount:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Recovery found a torn or corrupt record, or a segment header it couldn’t read, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"discarded the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"byteCount"},{"type":"text","text":" bytes from there to the end of the segment."}],"title":"DropReport.corruption(byteCount:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"corruption","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"byteCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"recordCount"},{"type":"text","text":" records, tracked within "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamps"},{"type":"text","text":", to disk failed (the disk is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"full, say, or segments that couldn’t be deleted fill the bound), so they are kept in memory"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only: delivered in this run if it lasts long"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"enough, lost if it ends first."}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/writefailed(recordcount:timestamps:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"writeFailed","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"recordCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"timestamps","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ClosedRange","preciseIdentifier":"s:SN","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Date","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4DateV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">)","kind":"text"}],"title":"DropReport.writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size, until they are delivered."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","kind":"symbol","title":"SegmentStore","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore","role":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/directory":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where the store keeps its segments."}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/directory","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"directory","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FilePath","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SystemPackage8FilePathV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"directory","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/directory"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/init(directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A store keeping events of every type the program declares with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":", and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library’s own, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directory"},{"type":"text","text":"; it recovers the records already there."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"directory"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"FilePath","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SystemPackage8FilePathV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"byteBound"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"segmentByteCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text",